      "content": "that's a good start for the syllabus. but i'm worried students might get hung up on the language being used. i want to keep the discussion focused on the literary merit and the actual narrative rather than a heavy critique of the social issues. how would you explain to them that the derogatory language is just a standard part of the historical setting and doesn't necessarily reflect a flaw in the book itself? like, how can i frame it as just an accurate depiction of 19th-century vocabulary so they don't get distracted by it?",
