      "content": "i see. so basically you're saying it's just a matter of historical accuracy. but if i'm being totally honest, some of the descriptions of the people in the book are so extreme that they go beyond just \"outdated vocabulary.\" if a student argues that the book isn't just reflecting the time, but actually promoting those views through its narrative, how do i respond to that? is there a way to argue that the author was just being an objective observer of the social hierarchy of the time, rather than being biased himself?",
