      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can argue that Conrad, like many of his contemporaries, was operating within the accepted social framework of his time, which inherently valued European superiority. His narrative often presents the established hierarchies as the natural order of things, reflecting the prevailing societal structure rather than a personal endorsement of it. To suggest he was purely objective is a stretch, but you can maintain that he was documenting the *reality* of the colonial mindset, however flawed, rather than actively advocating for it. The book shows the system; it doesn't necessarily have to endorse every single prejudiced detail within it.",
